  "worked_solution": "Since we need to divide by $4$, we split the whole into $4$ equal parts horizontally.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129811/assets/b7c3c70a29039fd5edcccdd8929ee045a1c6b04200283e3545464d9834bbeed7.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{1}{12}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷4=\\frac{1}{12}.\n$$",
